---
source: crates/orbit/src/app/cli_args.rs
expression: output
---
Run a one-off command in a new container on the Docker host.

Usage: orbit run [FLAGS] <SERVICE> [ARGS]…

Arguments:
  <SERVICE>  Service to run.
  [ARGS]…    Arguments passed to the container verbatim.

Flags:
      --rm                       Remove the container when it exits.
      --pull <PULL>              Pull images before starting.
                                 [possible values: always, missing, never]
  -e, --env <KEY=VALUE>          Set an environment variable in the container.
      --build                    Build the image before starting.
      --no-deps                  Don't start the service's dependencies.
  -d, --detach                   Run the container in the background and print
                                 its ID.
  -T, --no-tty                   Don't allocate a pseudo-TTY.
      --entrypoint <ENTRYPOINT>  Override the entrypoint of the image.
  -u, --user <USER>              Run as this user name or UID.
  -w, --workdir <PATH>           Working directory inside the container.
      --name <NAME>              Name the container.
  -P, --service-ports            Publish the service's ports to the host.
  -h, --help                     Print help

Global flags:
      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>    Set the log level.
                                 [possible values: error, warn, info, debug,
                                 trace]
                                 [env: ORBIT_LOG_LEVEL]
